{
  "kanda": "aranya",
  "sarga": 13,
  "title": "Sage Agastya directs Sri Rama to Panchavati",
  "sourceUrl": "https://www.valmikiramayan.net/utf8/aranya/sarga13/aranyasans13.htm",
  "romanUrl": "https://www.valmikiramayan.net/utf8/aranya/sarga13/aranyaitrans13.htm",
  "translator": "Desiraju Hanumanta Rao",
  "introduction": [
    "Rama requests Sage Agastya to indicate a place in the forest to make a residence during the days of exile. Sage Agastya foresees the next course of Ramayana, and orients his conversation around womanhood and Seetha. Then that sage informs Rama to proceed to Panchavati where Seetha will be delightful of its surroundings."
  ],
  "closing": [
    "इति वाल्मीकि रामायणे आदि काव्ये अरण्य काण्डे त्रयोदशः सर्गः",
    "Thus, this is the 13th chapter in Aranya Kanda of Valmiki Ramayana, the First Epic poem of India."
  ],
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "3.13.1",
      "label": "3.13.1",
      "numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "devanagari": "राम प्रीतो अस्मि भद्रम् ते परितुष्टो अस्मि लक्ष्मण |\nअभिवादयितुम् यन् माम् प्राप्तौ स्थः सह सीतया",
      "iast": "rāma prīto asmi bhadram te parituṣṭo asmi lakṣmaṇa |\nabhivādayitum yan mām prāptau sthaḥ saha sītayā",
      "translation": "\" I am delighted Rama, safe you be, oh Lakshmana, well-contended I am for you have come to pay respects to me along with Seetha.",
      "notes": [],
      "glosses": [
        {
          "itrans": "raama priitaH asmi",
          "iast": "rāma prītaḥ asmi",
          "devanagari": "राम प्रीतः अस्मि",
          "meaning": "oh, Rama, delighted, I am",
          "anvayaIndex": 0,
          "verseIndex": 0
        },
        {
          "itrans": "bhadram te",
          "iast": "bhadram te",
          "devanagari": "भद्रं ते",
          "meaning": "safe, you be",
          "anvayaIndex": 1,
          "verseIndex": 3
        },
        {
          "itrans": "pari tuSTAH asmi lakSmaNa",
          "iast": "pari tuṣṭAḥ asmi lakṣmaṇa",
          "devanagari": "परि तुष्ट्Aः अस्मि लक्ष्मण",
          "meaning": "well, contented, I am, Lakshmana",
          "anvayaIndex": 2,
          "verseIndex": null
        },
        {
          "itrans": "yat",
          "iast": "yat",
          "devanagari": "यत्",
          "meaning": "by which reason",
          "anvayaIndex": 3,
          "verseIndex": null
        },
        {
          "itrans": "siitayaa saha maam abhivaadayitum praaptau sthaH",
          "iast": "sītayā saha mām abhivādayitum prāptau sthaḥ",
          "devanagari": "सीतया सह मां अभिवादयितुं प्राप्तौ स्थः",
          "meaning": "with, Seetha, me, to pay respects, arrived, you have.",
          "anvayaIndex": 4,
          "verseIndex": 8
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "3.13.2",
      "label": "3.13.2",
      "numbers": [
        2
      ],
      "devanagari": "अध्व श्रमेण वाम् खेदो बाधते प्रचुर श्रमः |\nव्यक्तम् उत्कण्ठते वा अपि मैथिली जनक आत्मजा",
      "iast": "adhva śrameṇa vām khedo bādhate pracura śramaḥ |\nvyak{}tam ut{}kaṇṭhate vā api maithilī janaka ātmajā",
      "translation": "\"The well-worn trail of yours on pathway is strenuousness and painful for you two, and it is evident from the sweat above your necks, even much more for Janaka's daughter, Maithili.",
      "notes": [
        "The word <em>utkaṇṭha</em> is interpreted in two ways. One is <em>ut kaṇṭha</em> above neck, sides of face; the other being the anxiousness to get some rest. Thus, they are either wet with sweat or also anxious to get rest after a long trek in woods."
      ],
      "glosses": [
        {
          "itrans": "adhva shrameNa pracura shramaH",
          "iast": "adhva śrameṇa pracura śramaḥ",
          "devanagari": "अध्व श्रमेण प्रचुर श्रमः",
          "meaning": "pathway, strain of, much, strain",
          "anvayaIndex": 0,
          "verseIndex": null
        },
        {
          "itrans": "vaam baadhate",
          "iast": "vām bādhate",
          "devanagari": "वां बाधते",
          "meaning": "you two, it is painful",
          "anvayaIndex": 1,
          "verseIndex": 2
        },
        {
          "itrans": "janaka aatmajaa maithilii vaa api",
          "iast": "janaka ātmajā maithilī vā api",
          "devanagari": "जनक आत्मजा मैथिली वा अपि",
          "meaning": "Janaka's, daughter, Maithili, or, even",
          "anvayaIndex": 2,
          "verseIndex": 9
        },
        {
          "itrans": "vyaktam ut kaNThate",
          "iast": "vyaktam ut kaṇṭhate",
          "devanagari": "व्यक्तं उत् कण्ठते",
          "meaning": "evident, above, necks.",
          "anvayaIndex": 3,
          "verseIndex": 7
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "3.13.3",
      "label": "3.13.3",
      "numbers": [
        3
      ],
      "devanagari": "एषा च सुकुमारी च खेदैः च न विमानिता |\nप्राअज्य दोषम् वनम् प्रप्ता भर्तृ स्नेह प्रचोदिता",
      "iast": "eṣā ca sukumārī ca khedaiḥ ca na vimānitā |\nprāajya doṣam vanam praptā bhartṛ sneha pracoditā",
      "translation": "\"She is delicate and not discomforted by such distresses earlier, yet motivated by her friendship she came to these highly detrimental forests.",
      "notes": [],
      "glosses": [
        {
          "itrans": "sukumaarii ca",
          "iast": "sukumārī ca",
          "devanagari": "सुकुमारी च",
          "meaning": "delicate one, also",
          "anvayaIndex": 0,
          "verseIndex": 1
        },
        {
