    {
      "id": "3.13.4",
      "label": "3.13.4",
      "numbers": [
        4
      ],
      "devanagari": "यथा एषा रमते राम इह सीता तथा कुरु |\nदुष्करम् कृतवती एषा वने त्वाम् अभिगच्छ्हती",
      "iast": "yathā eṣā ramate rāma iha sītā tathā kuru |\nduṣkaram kṛtavatī eṣā vane tvām abhigacchhatī",
      "translation": "\"In which way Seetha takes delight in these forests, Rama, that you may ensure to her, for she has done an impossible deed in following you to forests, an impossible deed for womenfolk, in general.",
      "notes": [],
      "glosses": [
        {
          "itrans": "raama",
          "iast": "rāma",
          "devanagari": "राम",
          "meaning": "Rama",
          "anvayaIndex": 0,
          "verseIndex": 3
        },
        {
