          "meaning": "privileged, I am",
          "anvayaIndex": 3,
          "verseIndex": null
        },
        {
          "itrans": "anu gR^ihiitaH asmi",
          "iast": "anu gṛhītaḥ asmi",
          "devanagari": "अनु गृहीतः अस्मि",
          "meaning": "blessed, I am.",
          "anvayaIndex": 4,
          "verseIndex": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "3.13.11",
      "label": "3.13.11",
      "numbers": [
        11
      ],
      "devanagari": "किन्तु व्यादिश मे देशम् स उदकम् बहु काननम् |\nयत्र आश्रम पदम् कृत्वा वसेयम् निरतः सुखम्",
      "iast": "kintu vyādiśa me deśam sa udakam bahu kānanam |\nyatra āśrama padam kṛtvā vaseyam nirataḥ sukham",
      "translation": "\"But a place with water and many forests may please be shown, where I can reside happily and self-composedly on erecting a hermitage.\" Thus Rama asked the Sage Agastya.",
      "notes": [],
      "glosses": [
        {
          "itrans": "kintu",
          "iast": "kintu",
          "devanagari": "किन्तु",
          "meaning": "but",
