        },
        {
          "itrans": "yatra aashrama padam kR^itvaa",
          "iast": "yatra āśrama padam kṛtvā",
          "devanagari": "यत्र आश्रम पदं कृत्वा",
          "meaning": "where, hermitage's, threshold, on erecting",
          "anvayaIndex": 1,
          "verseIndex": 8
        },
        {
          "itrans": "desham",
          "iast": "deśam",
          "devanagari": "देशं",
          "meaning": "place",
          "anvayaIndex": 2,
          "verseIndex": 3
        },
        {
          "itrans": "sa udakam",
          "iast": "sa udakam",
          "devanagari": "स उदकं",
          "meaning": "with, water",
          "anvayaIndex": 3,
          "verseIndex": 4
        },
        {
          "itrans": "bahu kaananam",
          "iast": "bahu kānanam",
          "devanagari": "बहु काननं",
          "meaning": "many, forests",
          "anvayaIndex": 4,
          "verseIndex": 6
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "3.13.12",
      "label": "3.13.12",
      "numbers": [
        12
      ],
      "devanagari": "ततो अब्रवीत् मुनि श्रेष्ठः श्रुत्वा रामस्य भाषितम् |\nध्यात्वा मुहूर्तम् धर्मात्मा धीरो धीरतरम् वचः",
      "iast": "tato abravīt muni śreṣṭhaḥ śrutvā rāmasya bhāṣitam |\ndhyātvā muhūrtam dharmātmā dhīro dhīrataram vacaḥ",
      "translation": "Then that eminent sage Agastya on contemplating a while about what Rama has said, that virtuous and confident sage spoke more ideational word to Rama.",
      "notes": [
        "Rama wanted a place with 'many forests,' which is non-conditional to his exile. Some versions contain after <em>dharma ātmā</em> , and said <em>tato vāca vacaḥ subham</em>. This will not appear in critical or eastern recessions. For this <em>dīraḥ dhīra taram vacaḥ</em> , is there. It is said, that sage Agastya contemplated for a while, and envisioning the future of Seetha's abduction and Rama's elimination of Ravana etc by his yogic power, he said to Rama to stay at Panchavati. This is because, he himself is courageous sage in eliminating the demons, trusting that Rama also will do the same, he has shown a place which has many forests' around it, that too as Rama desired."
      ],
      "glosses": [
        {
          "itrans": "tataH",
          "iast": "tataḥ",
          "devanagari": "ततः",
          "meaning": "then",
          "anvayaIndex": 0,
          "verseIndex": 0
        },
        {
          "itrans": "dharmaatmaa",
          "iast": "dharmātmā",
          "devanagari": "धर्मात्मा",
          "meaning": "virtuous one",
          "anvayaIndex": 1,
          "verseIndex": 9
        },
        {
          "itrans": "dhiiraH",
          "iast": "dhīraḥ",
          "devanagari": "धीरः",
          "meaning": "confident one",
          "anvayaIndex": 2,
          "verseIndex": 10
        },
        {
          "itrans": "muni shreSThaH",
          "iast": "muni śreṣṭhaḥ",
          "devanagari": "मुनि श्रेष्ठः",
          "meaning": "sage, the eminent",
          "anvayaIndex": 3,
          "verseIndex": 2
        },
        {
          "itrans": "raamasya bhaaSitam vacaH shrutvaa",
          "iast": "rāmasya bhāṣitam vacaḥ śrutvā",
          "devanagari": "रामस्य भाषितं वचः श्रुत्वा",
          "meaning": "Rama's, said, saying, on hearing",
          "anvayaIndex": 4,
          "verseIndex": null
        },
        {
          "itrans": "dhyaatvaa muhuurtam",
          "iast": "dhyātvā muhūrtam",
          "devanagari": "ध्यात्वा मुहूर्तं",
          "meaning": "contemplated, a while",
          "anvayaIndex": 5,
          "verseIndex": 7
        },
        {
          "itrans": "dhiira taram vacaH abraviit",
          "iast": "dhīra taram vacaḥ abravīt",
          "devanagari": "धीर तरं वचः अब्रवीत्",
          "meaning": "intellectual [ideational,] more, word, said.",
          "anvayaIndex": 6,
          "verseIndex": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "3.13.13",
      "label": "3.13.13",
      "numbers": [
        13
      ],
      "devanagari": "इतो द्वि योजने तात बहु मूल फल उदकः |\nदेशो बहु मृगः श्रीमान् पंचवटि अभिविश्रुतः",
      "iast": "ito dvi yojane tāta bahu mūla phala udakaḥ |\ndeśo bahu mṛgaḥ śrīmān paṃcavaṭi abhiviśrutaḥ",
      "translation": "\"A most prosperous place called Panchavati is there at a distance of two yojana-s from here, oh, dear Rama, which is abundant with tubers, fruits, water, and many deer.\" Thus Agastya started to tell.",
      "notes": [],
      "glosses": [
        {
          "itrans": "taata",
          "iast": "tāta",
          "devanagari": "तात",
          "meaning": "oh, dear",
          "anvayaIndex": 0,
          "verseIndex": 3
        },
        {
          "itrans": "bahu muula phala udakaH",
          "iast": "bahu mūla phala udakaḥ",
          "devanagari": "बहु मूल फल उदकः",
          "meaning": "with many, tubers, fruits, waters",
          "anvayaIndex": 1,
          "verseIndex": 4
        },
        {
          "itrans": "bahu mR^igaH",
          "iast": "bahu mṛgaḥ",
          "devanagari": "बहु मृगः",
          "meaning": "with many, deer",
          "anvayaIndex": 2,
          "verseIndex": 9
        },
        {
          "itrans": "shriimaan",
          "iast": "śrīmān",
          "devanagari": "श्रीमान्",
          "meaning": "a prosperous one",
          "anvayaIndex": 3,
          "verseIndex": 11
        },
        {
          "itrans": "itaH dvi yojana",
          "iast": "itaḥ dvi yojana",
          "devanagari": "इतः द्वि योजन",
          "meaning": "from here, two yojana-s.",
          "anvayaIndex": 4,
          "verseIndex": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "3.13.14",
      "label": "3.13.14",
      "numbers": [
        14
      ],
      "devanagari": "तत्र गत्वा आश्रम पदम् कृत्वा सौमित्रिणा सह |\nरमस्व त्वम् पितुर् वाक्यम् यथा उक्तम् अनुपालयन्",
      "iast": "tatra gatvā āśrama padam kṛtvā saumitriṇā saha |\nramasva tvam pitur vākyam yathā uk{}tam anupālayan",
      "translation": "\"On your going there along with Saumitri, and on erecting a hermitage you may take delight in there complying the decreed order of your father.",
      "notes": [],
      "glosses": [
        {
          "itrans": "tvam saumitriNaa saha tatra gatvaa",
          "iast": "tvam saumitriṇā saha tatra gatvā",
          "devanagari": "त्वं सौमित्रिणा सह तत्र गत्वा",
          "meaning": "you, there, Soumitri, along with, on going, there",
          "anvayaIndex": 0,
          "verseIndex": null
        },
        {
          "itrans": "aashrama padam kR^itvaa",
          "iast": "āśrama padam kṛtvā",
          "devanagari": "आश्रम पदं कृत्वा",
          "meaning": "hermitage, on erecting",
          "anvayaIndex": 1,
          "verseIndex": 2
        },
        {
          "itrans": "yathaa uktam pituH vaakyam anupaalayan",
          "iast": "yathā uktam pituḥ vākyam anupālayan",
          "devanagari": "यथा उक्तं पितुः वाक्यं अनुपालयन्",
          "meaning": "as, decreed, father's, sentence [order], complying with",
          "anvayaIndex": 2,
          "verseIndex": 9
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "3.13.15",
      "label": "3.13.15",
      "numbers": [
        15
      ],
      "devanagari": "विदितो हि एष वृत्तांतो मम सर्वः तव अनघ |\nतपसः च प्रभावेण स्नेहाद् दशरथस्य च",
      "iast": "vidito hi eṣa vṛttāṃto mama sarvaḥ tava anagha |\ntapasaḥ ca prabhāveṇa snehād daśarathasya ca",
      "translation": "\"Indeed all of this episode of yours is known to me, oh, merited one, by the ability of my asceticism, and also by my friendship with Dasharatha.",
      "notes": [],
      "glosses": [
        {
          "itrans": "anagha",
          "iast": "anagha",
          "devanagari": "अनघ",
          "meaning": "oh, merited one",
          "anvayaIndex": 0,
          "verseIndex": 8
        },
        {
          "itrans": "tapasaH prabhaaveNa",
          "iast": "tapasaḥ prabhāveṇa",
          "devanagari": "तपसः प्रभावेण",
          "meaning": "by [my ascesis,] ability of",
          "anvayaIndex": 1,
          "verseIndex": 9
        },
        {
          "itrans": "snehaat dasharathasya ca",
          "iast": "snehāt daśarathasya ca",
          "devanagari": "स्नेहात् दशरथस्य च",
          "meaning": "iby my friendship, with Dasharatha, also",
          "anvayaIndex": 2,
          "verseIndex": 12
        },
        {
          "itrans": "tava eSa sarvaH vR^ittaantaH",
          "iast": "tava eṣa sarvaḥ vṛttāntaḥ",
          "devanagari": "तव एष सर्वः वृत्तान्तः",
          "meaning": "your, this, all of, episode",
          "anvayaIndex": 3,
          "verseIndex": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "3.13.16",
      "label": "3.13.16",
      "numbers": [
        16
      ],
      "devanagari": "हृदयस्थः च ते छ्हन्दो विज्ञातः तपसा मया |\nइह वासम् प्रतिज्ञाय मया सह तपो वने\nअतः च त्वाम् अहम् ब्रूमि गच्छ्ह पंचवटीम् इति |",
      "iast": "hṛdayasthaḥ ca te chhando viGYātaḥ tapasā mayā |\niha vāsam pratiGYāya mayā saha tapo vane\nataḥ ca tvām aham brūmi gacchha paṃcavaṭīm iti |",
      "translation": "\"I am in the know of your heartfelt certitude by my ascesis, thereby I wish to advise you to go to Panchavati, though I said that you may dwell in these ascetic-woods along with me.",
      "notes": [],
      "glosses": [
        {
          "itrans": "te hR^idayaH sthaH ca ChandaH",
          "iast": "te hṛdayaḥ sthaḥ ca chandaḥ",
          "devanagari": "ते हृदयः स्थः च छन्दः",
          "meaning": "your, in heart, abided, certitude",
          "anvayaIndex": 0,
          "verseIndex": null
        },
        {
          "itrans": "ataH",
          "iast": "ataḥ",
          "devanagari": "अतः",
          "meaning": "thereby",
          "anvayaIndex": 1,
          "verseIndex": 14
        },
        {
          "itrans": "maya saha iha tapaH vane",
          "iast": "maya saha iha tapaḥ vane",
          "devanagari": "मय सह इह तपः वने",
          "meaning": "me, along with, in ascetic, woods",
          "anvayaIndex": 2,
          "verseIndex": 7
        },
        {
          "itrans": "vaasam pratiGYaaya",
          "iast": "vāsam pratiGYāya",
          "devanagari": "वासं प्रतिGYआय",
          "meaning": "dwelling, I said",
          "anvayaIndex": 3,
          "verseIndex": 8
        },
        {
          "itrans": "pancavaTiim gacCha iti tvaam aham bruumi",
          "iast": "pancavaṭīm gaccha iti tvām aham brūmi",
          "devanagari": "पन्चवटीं गच्छ इति त्वां अहं ब्रूमि",
          "meaning": "to Panchavati, you go, thus as, to you, I am, telling [advising.]",
          "anvayaIndex": 4,
          "verseIndex": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "3.13.17",
      "label": "3.13.17",
      "numbers": [
        17
      ],
      "devanagari": "स हि रम्यो वनोद्देशो मैथिली तत्र रंस्यते\nस देशः श्लाघनीयः च न अतिदूरे च राघव |",
      "iast": "sa hi ramyo vanoddeśo maithilī tatra raṃsyate\nsa deśaḥ ślāghanīyaḥ ca na atidūre ca rāghava |",
      "translation": "\"That woodland will be delightful, isn't it Raghava, for it is praiseworthy and not very far off from here, and Seetha can take delight in there.",
      "notes": [],
      "glosses": [
        {
          "itrans": "raaghava",
          "iast": "rāghava",
          "devanagari": "राघव",
          "meaning": "oh, Raghava",
          "anvayaIndex": 0,
          "verseIndex": 14
        },
        {
          "itrans": "saH vanoddeshaH ramyaH hi",
          "iast": "saḥ vanoddeśaḥ ramyaḥ hi",
          "devanagari": "सः वनोद्देशः रम्यः हि",
          "meaning": "that, woodland, are delightful, isn't it",
          "anvayaIndex": 1,
          "verseIndex": 0
        },
        {
          "itrans": "saH deshaH shlaaghaniiyaH ca",
          "iast": "saḥ deśaḥ ślāghanīyaḥ ca",
          "devanagari": "सः देशः श्लाघनीयः च",
          "meaning": "that, place, is praiseworthy, also",
          "anvayaIndex": 2,
          "verseIndex": 7
        },
        {
          "itrans": "na ati duure ca",
          "iast": "na ati dūre ca",
          "devanagari": "न अति दूरे च",
          "meaning": "not, very, far off, also",
          "anvayaIndex": 3,
          "verseIndex": 11
        },
        {
          "itrans": "maithilii tatra ramsyate",
          "iast": "maithilī tatra ramsyate",
          "devanagari": "मैथिली तत्र रम्स्यते",
          "meaning": "Maithili, therein, can take delight.",
          "anvayaIndex": 4,
          "verseIndex": 4
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "3.13.18",
      "label": "3.13.18, 19",
      "numbers": [
        18,
        19
      ],
      "devanagari": "गोदावर्याः समीपे च मैथिली तत्र रंस्यते\nप्राज्य मूल फलैः चैव नाना द्विज गणैर् युतः |\nविविक्तः च महाबाहो पुण्यो रम्यः तथैव च",
      "iast": "godāvaryāḥ samīpe ca maithilī tatra raṃsyate\nprājya mūla phalaiḥ caiva nānā dvija gaṇair yutaḥ |\nvivik{}taḥ ca mahābāho puṇyo ramyaḥ tathaiva ca",
      "translation": "\"There Maithili will take delight nearby River Godavari, and it is with abundant tubers, fruits, various are its bird flocks, and it is very reclusive too, oh, great dextrous Rama, further it is meritorious and appealing.",
      "notes": [],
      "glosses": [
        {
          "itrans": "maithilii tatra godaavaryaaH samiipe ramsyate",
          "iast": "maithilī tatra godāvaryāḥ samīpe ramsyate",
          "devanagari": "मैथिली तत्र गोदावर्याः समीपे रम्स्यते",
          "meaning": "Maithili, there, at Godavari, nearby, takes delights",
          "anvayaIndex": 0,
          "verseIndex": 0
        },
        {
          "itrans": "praajya muula phalaiH caiva",
          "iast": "prājya mūla phalaiḥ caiva",
          "devanagari": "प्राज्य मूल फलैः चैव",
          "meaning": "bounteous, tubers, fruits, also",
          "anvayaIndex": 1,
          "verseIndex": 6
        },
        {
          "itrans": "naanaa dvija gaNaiH yutaH",
          "iast": "nānā dvija gaṇaiḥ yutaḥ",
          "devanagari": "नाना द्विज गणैः युतः",
          "meaning": "various, bird, flocks",
          "anvayaIndex": 2,
          "verseIndex": 10
        },
        {
          "itrans": "mahaa baahuH",
          "iast": "mahā bāhuḥ",
          "devanagari": "महा बाहुः",
          "meaning": "great, dexterous Rama",
          "anvayaIndex": 3,
          "verseIndex": 16
        },
        {
          "itrans": "vi viktaH ca",
          "iast": "vi viktaḥ ca",
          "devanagari": "वि विक्तः च",
          "meaning": "verily, reclusive, too",
          "anvayaIndex": 4,
          "verseIndex": 14
        },
        {
          "itrans": "puNyaH tathaa eva ca",
          "iast": "puṇyaḥ tathā eva ca",
          "devanagari": "पुण्यः तथा एव च",
          "meaning": "meritorious, like that, even, also ramyaH = appealing one.",
          "anvayaIndex": 5,
          "verseIndex": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "3.13.20",
      "label": "3.13.20",
      "numbers": [
        20
      ],
      "devanagari": "भवान् अपि सदाचारः च शक्तः च परिरक्षणे |\nअपि च अत्र वसन् राम तापसान् पालयिष्यसि",
      "iast": "bhavān api sadācāraḥ ca śak{}taḥ ca parirakṣaṇe |\napi ca atra vasan rāma tāpasān pālayiṣyasi",
      "translation": "\"Even you, Rama, with your good deportment are capable to safeguard the hermits while residing there.",
      "notes": [],
      "glosses": [
        {
          "itrans": "bhavaan api sat aacaaraH",
          "iast": "bhavān api sat ācāraḥ",
          "devanagari": "भवान् अपि सत् आचारः",
          "meaning": "you are, even, with good, bearing",
          "anvayaIndex": 0,
          "verseIndex": null
        },
        {
          "itrans": "pari rakSaNe shaktaH",
          "iast": "pari rakṣaṇe śaktaḥ",
          "devanagari": "परि रक्षणे शक्तः",
          "meaning": "to safeguard, you are capable",
          "anvayaIndex": 1,
          "verseIndex": null
        },
        {
          "itrans": "api ca",
          "iast": "api ca",
          "devanagari": "अपि च",
          "meaning": "even also",
          "anvayaIndex": 2,
          "verseIndex": 7
        },
        {
          "itrans": "atra vasan",
          "iast": "atra vasan",
          "devanagari": "अत्र वसन्",
          "meaning": "there, while residing",
          "anvayaIndex": 3,
          "verseIndex": 9
        },
        {
          "itrans": "raama",
          "iast": "rāma",
          "devanagari": "राम",
          "meaning": "Rama",
          "anvayaIndex": 4,
          "verseIndex": 11
        },
        {
          "itrans": "taapasaan paalayiSyasi",
          "iast": "tāpasān pālayiṣyasi",
          "devanagari": "तापसान् पालयिष्यसि",
          "meaning": "hermits, you can protect.",
          "anvayaIndex": 5,
          "verseIndex": 12
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "3.13.21",
      "label": "3.13.21",
      "numbers": [
        21
      ],
      "devanagari": "एतत् आलक्ष्यते वीर मधूकानाम् महत् वनम् |\nउत्तरेण अस्य गंतव्यम् न्यग्रोधम् अपि गच्छ्हता",
      "iast": "etat ālakṣyate vīra madhūkānām mahat vanam |\nuttareṇa asya gaṃtavyam nyagrodham api gacchhatā",
      "translation": "\"Oh, brave one, you see this great forest of flower-liquor trees, you have to proceed north of it and advance towards a banyan tree.",
      "notes": [],
      "glosses": [
        {
          "itrans": "viira",
          "iast": "vīra",
          "devanagari": "वीर",
          "meaning": "oh, brave one",
          "anvayaIndex": 0,
          "verseIndex": 2
        },
